"""
# Lock-Free Parallel Claiming, Multi-Worker Step-5 Codegen, and Concurrent Cache Writers

Regression specification proving:
1. Multi-worker claiming over a 500+ item queue executes locklessly with zero
   duplicate claims, zero lost items, zero `.lock` files, O(N) (not O(N^2))
   probes per worker across unit-pick, HIR/MIR shard schedules, and parse-fiber rings,
   and crash-safe pre-published per-owner / `+fork` tree claim directories.
2. Parallel backend object compilation and staged codegen dispatch >= 2 concurrent
   workers when `--threads 4` and sufficient host memory headroom are present,
   terminate promptly (< 2s) with real compiler diagnostics when a C unit fails,
   and use responsive 5-15ms adaptive reap polling and O(N) SMF object assembly.
3. Concurrent cache writers (`BuildCache`, `postbuild_coordinator_v1`, `.fpc`,
   `.spab`) write via PID+sequence-unique temp files + atomic publish/rename,
   merge sibling `BuildCache` updates with matching reverse-reference generation
   receipts and pruning tombstones, and never create global `.lock` files.
"""
# @req REQ-COMPILER-DRIVER-LOCKFREE-PARALLEL-001
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/driver_hir_recovery.spl 80%
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/driver_worker_surface_closure_v1.spl 60%
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/driver_build/native_mir_shard.spl 60%
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/driver_build/native_staged_codegen.spl 80%
# @cover src/compiler/70.backend/backend/runtime_c_compile_pool_v1.spl 80%
# @cover src/compiler/80.driver/cache/postbuild_coordinator_v1.spl 80%

